            "creator": "luke",
            "id": 103986,
            "is_private": false,
            "tags": [],
            "text": "Thanks. This looks like it may be the right change, but the place to make it is in `noweb/compiler.nw`. The explanation should go in the supporting text rather than a comment.",
            "bug_id": 19252,
            "count": 2,
            "creation_time": "2026-10-28T19:16:27Z"
          },
          {
            "creation_time": "2026-10-28T22:15:52Z",
            "creator": "kevinushey",
            "bug_id": 19252,
            "text": "Created attachment 3966\npatch v2: fix made in compiler.nw, cmp.R regenerated\n\nThanks -- updated patch attached (against r90764). The change is now in noweb/compiler.nw, with the explanation in the supporting text after the INCLNKSTK/DECLNKSTK chunks, and cmp.R is regenerated with notangle.\n\nOne difference from the first version: the argument context is only used for non-top-level complex assignments, where INCLNKSTK has already changed the stack. At top level the right hand side is computed before anything is on the stack, so the code generated for top-level assignments is unchanged. I also added a test for next in a for loop, which corrupts the loop state instead of crashing (\"invalid sequence argument in for loop\").",
            "is_markdown": false,
